That's how I implemented the shirt - it is only an issue if
it is visible.  It can indeed have a material benefit if it
is enchanted, however: it is just like any other shirt, and
can be enchanted and worn under armor to provide extra AC.
Starting it out as cursed sounds fun, too, though.

> > Guards: Guards who see a Convict will recognize him
> > from wanted posters and immediately become hostile.
>
> By guards, do you mean vault guards only, or Minetown Watch
> also?  (Personally, I think it should be both, as that makes the
> role more distinctive.)

I had coded it only for the watchmen of Minetown, but
extending it to vault guards sounds like a fun addition.

> > Weapon Skills:
>
> > Basic: mace, short sword, quarterstaff, heavy iron ball,
> >    two-weapon combat
> > Skilled: dagger, dart, hammer, sling
> > Expert: club, knife, pick-axe, unarmed combat
